  "limitations": [
    "Finite synthetic native timings; no universal,live-provider,concurrent,production-weighted or physical ARM throughput assertion.",
    "No individual primary control exceeded1.05, so the prescribed follow-up selected no cases. All primary control timings remain retained.",
    "Initial causal test compilation used an unimported enum; that failed attempt is retained. The correction and subsequent review-driven test expansion did not alter runtime code.",
    "Strict lint identified two unnecessary Vec identity conversions in a new test. Removing them changed no runtime source or test semantics. Final lint/format/MSRV and four causal tests pass; optimized native/ARM suites retain their earlier source attribution.",
    "The initial C fixture incorrectly assumed full bucket weight under histogram_sum and no idelta warning for counter inputs. Accepted and candidate engines reproduced the same behavior. Corrected raw histogram queries pass on both; unchanged Rust unit and performance evidence is retained.",
    "The fresh-copy unit baseline is independent for successful output/allocation checks; cancellation phases are tested by injected actual work/release events.",
    "Reuse is an optimization boundary, not a language restriction. Varying capacity,custom bounds and incoming integer histograms continue through existing supported paths."
  ]
